<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2018-11315>
  dcterms:description "The Local HTTP API in Radio Thermostat CT50 and CT80 1.04.84 and below products allows unauthorized access via a DNS rebinding attack. This can result in remote device temperature control, as demonstrated by a tstat t_heat request that accesses a device purchased in the Spring of 2018, and sets a home's target temperature to 95 degrees Fahrenheit. This vulnerability might be described as an addendum to CVE-2013-4860." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:thermostat ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/radiothermostat/ct50> ;
