<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2018-7580>
  dcterms:description "Philips Hue is vulnerable to a Denial of Service attack. Sending a SYN flood on port tcp/80 will freeze Philips Hue's hub and it will stop responding. The \"hub\" will stop operating and be frozen until the flood stops. During the flood, the user won't be able to turn on/off the lights, and all of the hub's functionality will be unresponsive. The cloud service also won't work with the hub." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:lighting ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/philips/hue> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/philips/hue_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2018-7580_lighting> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "7.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-400> ;
  hkg:published "2020-12-21"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2018-7580" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2018-7698>
  dcterms:description "An issue was discovered in D-Link mydlink+ 3.8.5 build 259 for DCS-933L 1.05.04 and DCS-934L 1.05.04 devices. The mydlink+ app sends the username and password for connected D-Link cameras (such as DCS-933L and DCS-934L) unencrypted from the app to the camera, allowing attackers to obtain these credentials and gain control of the camera including the ability to view the camera's stream and make changes without the user's knowledge." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/d-link/mydlink%5C%2B> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2018-7698_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.0" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-522> ;
  hkg:published "2018-03-05"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2018-7698" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2018-8072>
  dcterms:description "An issue was discovered on EDIMAX IC-3140W through 3.06, IC-5150W through 3.09, and IC-6220DC through 3.06 devices. The ipcam_cgi binary contains a stack-based buffer overflow that is possible to trigger from a remote unauthenticated /camera-cgi/public/getsysyeminfo.cgi?action=VALUE_HERE HTTP request: if the VALUE_HERE length is more than 0x400 (1024), it is possible to overwrite other values located on the stack due to an incorrect use of the strcpy() function." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/edimax/ic-3140w> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/edimax/ic-3140w_firmware> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/edimax/ic-5150w> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/edimax/ic-5150w_firmware> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/edimax/ic-6220dc> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/edimax/ic-6220dc_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2018-8072_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.0" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-787> ;
  hkg:published "2018-04-26"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2018-8072" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2018-9070>
  dcterms:description "For the Lenovo Smart Assistant Android app versions earlier than 12.1.82, an attacker with physical access to the smart speaker can, by pressing a specific button sequence, enter factory test mode and enable a web service intended for testing the device. As with most test modes, this provides extra privileges, including changing settings and running code. Lenovo Smart Assistant is an Amazon Alexa-enabled smart speaker developed by Lenovo." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:smartspeakers ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/lenovo/smart_assistant> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2018-9070_smartspeakers> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "6.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.0" ;
  hkg:published "2018-07-13"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2018-9070" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2018-9995>
  dcterms:description "TBK DVR4104 and DVR4216 devices, as well as Novo, CeNova, QSee, Pulnix, XVR 5 in 1, Securus, Night OWL, DVR Login, HVR Login, and MDVR Login, which run re-branded versions of the original TBK DVR4104 and DVR4216 series, allow remote attackers to bypass authentication via a \"Cookie: uid=admin\" header, as demonstrated by a device.rsp?opt=user&cmd=list request that provides credentials within JSON data in a response." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/tbkvision/tbk-dvr4104> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/tbkvision/tbk-dvr4104_firmware> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/tbkvision/tbk-dvr4216> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/tbkvision/tbk-dvr4216_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2018-9995_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "9.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.0" ;
  hkg:published "2018-04-10"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2018-9995" .

