<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-24046>
  dcterms:description "This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Sonos One Speaker prior to 3.4.1 (S2 systems) and 11.2.13 build 57923290 (S1 systems). Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability. The specific flaw exists within the anacapd daemon. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of user-supplied data, which can result in an integer underflow before writing to memory. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root. Was ZDI-CAN-15828." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:smartspeakers ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/sonos/one> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/sonos/s1> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/sonos/s2> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-24046_smartspeakers> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-191> ;
  hkg:published "2022-02-18"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2022-24046" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-24049>
  dcterms:description "This vulnerability allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Sonos One Speaker prior to 3.4.1 (S2 systems) and 11.2.13 build 57923290 (S1 systems). Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability. The specific flaw exists within the ALAC audio codec. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root. Was ZDI-CAN-15798." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:smartspeakers ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/sonos/one> ;
