<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-32504>
  dcterms:description "An issue was discovered on certain Nuki Home Solutions devices. The code used to parse the JSON objects received from the WebSocket service provided by the device leads to a stack buffer overflow. An attacker would be able to exploit this to gain arbitrary code execution on a KeyTurner device. This affects Nuki Smart Lock 3.0 before 3.3.5 and 2.0 before 2.12.4, as well as Nuki Bridge v1 before 1.22.0 and v2 before 2.13.2." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:doorlock ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-32504_doorlock> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "9.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-120> ;
  hkg:published "2024-05-14"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2022-32504" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-32505>
  dcterms:description "An issue was discovered on certain Nuki Home Solutions devices. It is possible to send multiple BLE malformed packets to block some of the functionality and reboot the device. This affects Nuki Smart Lock 3.0 before 3.3.5 and Nuki Smart Lock 2.0 before 2.12.4." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:doorlock ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-32505_doorlock> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "7.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-400> ;
  hkg:published "2024-05-14"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2022-32505" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-32506>
  dcterms:description "An issue was discovered on certain Nuki Home Solutions devices. An attacker with physical access to the circuit board could use the SWD debug features to control the execution of code on the processor and debug the firmware, as well as read or alter the content of the internal and external flash memory. This affects Nuki Smart Lock 3.0 before 3.3.5, Nuki Smart Lock 2.0 before 2.12.4, as well as Nuki Bridge v1 before 1.22.0 and v2 before 2.13.2." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:doorlock ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-32506_doorlock> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "6.4"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-1263> ;
  hkg:published "2024-05-14"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2022-32506" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-32507>
  dcterms:description "An issue was discovered on certain Nuki Home Solutions devices. Some BLE commands, which should have been designed to be only called from privileged accounts, could also be called from unprivileged accounts. This demonstrates that no access controls were implemented for the different BLE commands across the different accounts. This affects Nuki Smart Lock 3.0 before 3.3.5 and Nuki Smart Lock 2.0 before 2.12.4." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:doorlock ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-32507_doorlock> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-284> ;
  hkg:published "2024-05-14"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2022-32507" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-32509>
  dcterms:description "An issue was discovered on certain Nuki Home Solutions devices. Lack of certificate validation on HTTP communications allows attackers to intercept and tamper data. This affects Nuki Smart Lock 3.0 before 3.3.5, Nuki Bridge v1 before 1.22.0 and Nuki Bridge v2 before 2.13.2." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:doorlock ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-32509_doorlock> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
