<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-33194>
  dcterms:description "Four OS command injection vulnerabilities exist in the XCMD testWifiAP functionality of Abode Systems, Inc. iota All-In-One Security Kit 6.9X and 6.9Z. A XCMD can lead to arbitrary command execution. An attacker can send a sequence of malicious commands to trigger these vulnerabilities.This vulnerability focuses on the unsafe use of the `WL_Key` and `WL_DefaultKeyID` configuration values in the function located at offset `0x1c7d28` of firmware 6.9Z , and even more specifically on the command execution occuring at offset `0x1c7f6c`." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:alarms ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/goabode/iota_all-in-one_security_kit_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-33194_alarms> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "10.0"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-78> ;
  hkg:published "2022-10-25"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2022-33194" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-33195>
  dcterms:description "Four OS command injection vulnerabilities exist in the XCMD testWifiAP functionality of Abode Systems, Inc. iota All-In-One Security Kit 6.9X and 6.9Z. A XCMD can lead to arbitrary command execution. An attacker can send a sequence of malicious commands to trigger these vulnerabilities.This vulnerability focuses on the unsafe use of the `WL_DefaultKeyID` in the function located at offset `0x1c7d28` of firmware 6.9Z, and even more specifically on the command execution occuring at offset `0x1c7fac`." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:alarms ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/goabode/iota_all-in-one_security_kit_firmware> ;
