<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-35878>
  dcterms:description "Four format string injection vulnerabilities exist in the UPnP logging functionality of Abode Systems, Inc. iota All-In-One Security Kit 6.9Z and 6.9X. A specially-crafted UPnP negotiation can lead to memory corruption, information disclosure, and denial of service. An attacker can host a malicious UPnP service to trigger these vulnerabilities.This vulnerability arises from format string injection via `ST` and `Location` HTTP response headers, as used within the `DoEnumUPnPService` action handler." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:alarms ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/goabode/iota_all-in-one_security_kit_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2022-35878_alarms> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-134> ;
  hkg:published "2022-10-25"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2022-35878" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2022-35879>
  dcterms:description "Four format string injection vulnerabilities exist in the UPnP logging functionality of Abode Systems, Inc. iota All-In-One Security Kit 6.9Z and 6.9X. A specially-crafted UPnP negotiation can lead to memory corruption, information disclosure, and denial of service. An attacker can host a malicious UPnP service to trigger these vulnerabilities.This vulnerability arises from format string injection via `controlURL` XML tag, as used within the `DoUpdateUPnPbyService` action handler." ;
