<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2023-46889>
  dcterms:description "Meross MSH30Q 4.5.23 is vulnerable to Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information. During the device setup phase, the MSH30Q creates an unprotected Wi-Fi access point. In this phase, MSH30Q needs to connect to the Internet through a Wi-Fi router. This is why MSH30Q asks for the Wi-Fi network name (SSID) and the Wi-Fi network password. When the user enters the password, the transmission of the Wi-Fi password and name between the MSH30Q and mobile application is observed in the Wi-Fi network. Although the Wi-Fi password is encrypted, a part of the decryption algorithm is public so we complemented the missing parts to decrypt it." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:thermostat ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/meross/msh30q> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/meross/msh30q_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2023-46889_thermostat> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "5.7"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-319> ;
  hkg:published "2024-01-23"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2023-46889" .

