<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2024-39351>
  dcterms:description "A vulnerability regarding improper neutralization of special elements used in an OS command ('OS Command Injection') is found in the NTP configuration. This allows remote authenticated users with administrator privileges to execute arbitrary commands via unspecified vectors. The following models with Synology Camera Firmware versions before 1.0.7-0298 may be affected: BC500 and TC500." ;
