<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2024-6246>
  dcterms:description "Wyze Cam v3 Realtek Wi-Fi Driver Heap-Based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Wyze Cam v3 IP cameras. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the Realtek Wi-Fi kernel module. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a heap-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the kernel. Was ZDI-CAN-22310." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2024-6246_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-122> ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-787> ;
  hkg:published "2024-11-22"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2024-6246" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2024-6247>
  dcterms:description "Wyze Cam v3 Wi-Fi SSID OS Command Injection Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows physically present attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Wyze Cam v3 IP cameras. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the handling of SSIDs embedded in scanned QR codes. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of a user-supplied string before using it to execute a system call. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root. Was ZDI-CAN-22337." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2024-6247_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "6.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.0" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-78> ;
  hkg:published "2024-11-22"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2024-6247" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2024-6248>
  dcterms:description "Wyze Cam v3 Cloud Infrastructure Improper Authentication Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Wyze Cam v3 IP cameras. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the run_action_batch endpoint of the cloud infrastructure. The issue results from the use of the device's MAC address as a sole credential for authentication. An attacker can leverage this in conjunction with other vulnerabilities to execute arbitrary code in the context of root. Was ZDI-CAN-22393." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2024-6248_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "7.5"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.0" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-287> ;
  hkg:published "2024-11-22"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2024-6248" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2024-6249>
  dcterms:description "Wyze Cam v3 TCP Traffic Handling Stack-Based Buffer Overflow Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows network-adjacent attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Wyze Cam v3 IP cameras. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the TUTK P2P library. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of the length of user-supplied data prior to copying it to a fixed-length stack-based buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of root. Was ZDI-CAN-22419." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/wyze/cam_v3_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2024-6249_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.0" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-121> ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-787> ;
  hkg:published "2024-11-22"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2024-6249" .

