<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2025-31700>
  dcterms:description "A vulnerability has been found in Dahua products.\n\nAttackers could exploit a buffer overflow vulnerability by sending specially crafted malicious packets, potentially causing service disruption (e.g., crashes) or remote code execution (RCE). Some devices may have deployed protection mechanisms such as Address Space Layout Randomization (ASLR), which reduces the likelihood of successful RCE exploitation. However, denial-of-service (DoS) attacks remain a concern." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:cameras ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2025-31700_cameras> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "8.1"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-120> ;
  hkg:published "2025-07-23"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2025-31700" .

