<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2026-38740>
  dcterms:description "Foscam VD1 Video Doorbell before V5.3.13_1072 is vulnerable to Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information. The device transmits sensitive Session Description Protocol (SDP), including ICE credentials and candidates, in cleartext over network interfaces. An attacker with network visibility can intercept these credentials to hijack media streams or authenticate to Foscam's TURN/relay infrastructure to forward arbitrary traffic at the vendor's expense." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:doorbell ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2026-38740_doorbell> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "5.3"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-319> ;
  hkg:published "2026-05-14"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2026-38740" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2026-4149>
  dcterms:description "Sonos Era 300 SMB Response Out-Of-Bounds Access Remote Code Execution Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code on affected installations of Sonos Era 300. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the handling of the DataOffset field within SMB responses. The issue results from the lack of proper validation of user-supplied data, which can result in a memory access past the end of an allocated buffer. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to execute code in the context of the kernel. Was ZDI-CAN-28345." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:smartspeakers ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/sonos/era_300> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/sonos/era_300_firmware> ;
  hkg:assignment <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/assignment/CVE-2026-4149_smartspeakers> ;
  hkg:cvssScore "9.8"^^xsd:decimal ;
  hkg:cvssVersion "3.1" ;
  hkg:hasWeakness <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cwe/CWE-119> ;
  hkg:published "2026-04-11"^^xsd:date ;
  rdf:type hkg:Vulnerability ;
  rdfs:label "CVE-2026-4149" .

<https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/cve/CVE-2026-4155>
  dcterms:description "ChargePoint Home Flex Inclusion of Sensitive Information in Source Code Information Disclosure Vulnerability. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to disclose sensitive information on affected installations of ChargePoint Home Flex charging stations. Authentication is not required to exploit this vulnerability.\n\nThe specific flaw exists within the genpw script. The issue results from the inclusion of a secret cryptographic seed value within the script. An attacker can leverage this vulnerability to disclose stored credentials, leading to further compromise. Was ZDI-CAN-26340." ;
  hkg:affectsCategory hiot:ev_charging ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/chargepoint/home_flex_cph50> ;
  hkg:affectsProduct <https://w3id.org/homeiot/kg/product/chargepoint/home_flex_cph50_firmware> ;
